in a previous mass effect lore video  about the first contact war  we mentioned that in the aftermath of  the conflict a few pro-human groups  sprung up  one of those groups is cerberus which  you'll likely hear a handful of times in  mass effect 1.  it becomes a far more prominent name in  the later mass effect games  so it's worth diving into the  organization's history if you're  enjoying our mass effect lore series be  sure to like this video  subscribe to the channel as well to get  more mass effect content  like our mass effect legendary edition  video review  though cerberus isn't founded until  after the first contact war  its origins are connected to the  conflict in the final moments of the war  the turians pushed the human alliance  back to shangsuke general williams led  the resistance against the turians  enlisting the aid of three mercenaries  jack harper eva correa and ben hislop  the trio managed to capture turian  general desolus arturius  yup arturius like sarah and arturius  don't worry  we'll get to that anyway jack takes the  lead on interrogating desolace learning  that the turian is not there to take  part in the ongoing war  instead desolace is searching for an  artifact hidden in a research vessel  that crashed onto the human colonized  world in the midst of the first contact  war  using a data pad on decilis the  mercenaries mislead a group of turians  searching for the artifact into a trap  ava is assigned to watch over desolace  and the rest of the turian prisoners  while jack and ben use the turian's data  to pinpoint the location of the artifact  and go to investigate the duo find the  artifact when ben approaches it it  activates and ensnares bin in a  mysterious energy  though jack is able to pull bin away the  artifact then emits a brilliant light  the resulting explosion envelops ben  puts jack into a coma  and distracts ava just long enough for  the turian prisoners to escape  desolace captures jack and eva and takes  the still intact artifact in for steady  jack awakens weeks later under guard in  a turian prison he and eva are being  overseen by saren desola's brother  saren tells the two that the war between  the turians and humans is now over  and both jack and eva are being traded  back to the alliance  in exchange for turin prisoners not been  though because apparently  ben is dead after the exchange goes  through  jack asks general williams how he plans  to go after desolus  still facing backlash over being the  first human to ever surrender to an  alien force  william's hands are tied he can't order  an investigation into deathless even if  he wanted to  however he does give jack and eva his  personal ship and alludes the two  should go after decilis and stop him  jack starts having visions of a coming  destruction at the hands of synthetics  and tells ava that he is now  linked to the artifact he can feel its  presence and he knows it's on ilium as  humans are still new to citadel space  the two don't know how to work the  technology on ilium but then jack's eyes  begin to glow and he suddenly perfectly  understands  how to work the alien technology before  they can reach the artifact sarin and  deceleus guards ambush the pair  one is revealed to be ben still alive  and transformed into a cybernetic  creature  saren and desolace then joined the fray  capturing jack and ava once again  at this point jack's eyes have fully  transformed taking on a cybernetic  appearance  wondering why jack's transformation is  so different from ben's full-body  metamorphosis  the turians decide to bring jack and eva  back to a lab on palavin  the turian home world jack ava and ben  become the first humans to ever step  foot on the planet  jack and eva are each imprisoned  separately and jack continues to have  visions related to the artifact which  only become more vivid after he sees  a monolith that desolus is attempting to  unearth on palavin  like the artifact the monolith can  transform organics into cybernetic  creatures like ben  the monolith can just do it on a larger  scale desolace hopes to use the monolith  to transform the entire turian species  making them all into powerful cybernetic  super soldiers  eventually jack's connection to the  artifact reveals to him the truth  the monolith will enslave the turian  race not just transform them  after convincing sarin of this jack ava  and sarin team together to prevent  decilis dooming the turians  in the battle ben is killed for real  this time eva is mortally wounded the  monolith is destroyed and desolace is  knocked out  jack carries ava away and saren seals  his brother and the remains of the  monolith away in order to prevent anyone  else  learning about it following a memorial  service for ava and ben  jack comes to the revelation that  humanity is ill-prepared to handle the  threats in the milky way galaxy  which is full of more dangers than  humans realize in his mind  the only way to prevent humanity's  destruction is to ensure that humans  become the most  dominant species in the galaxy he writes  the cerberus manifesto which details his  goals for achieving human supremacy  and begins building an organization  having no idea as to the identity of the  manifesto's author  the human alliance simply refers to the  creator of cerberus as  an elusive man the name sticks and jack  harper becomes  the elusive man the elusive man  structures cerberus around the idea of  the three-headed dog of greek myth  the organization exists to protect  humanity from all threats both known  and unknown the group is divided into  three separate cells each of which is  further divided into individual  projects that are overseen by project  leads  all projects run independently of each  other reporting to the elusive man  directly  as such there's no way for one project  to rat on the rest of the organization  as evidenced by miranda lawson who is  the lead for project lazarus  not knowing about the projects behind  subject zero or the overlord vi  so if a project or an entire cellus  compromise the elusive man can cut them  off and preserve the rest of the  organization  of course this makes it somewhat easy to  take down cerberus defeat the elusive  man and the whole organization crumbles  as such the elusive man remains in  hiding secretly speaking to his project  leads on encrypted channels  not many have seen his face and even  fewer have actually spoken to him in  person  the other issue with this structure is  that cells are so independent they can  easily break off from cerberus  throughout the trilogy you'll regularly  hear about project leads that went rogue  emitting crucial details about what they  were doing in the reports to the elusive  man some leads went even further than  that like  literally traveled further you can find  cerberus operatives in mass effect  andromeda  having traveled to a whole other galaxy  to continue their work without fear of  the elusive man knowing about their  projects  though cerberus only maintains a few  projects at a time the organization has  operatives  everywhere the one exception is the  quarian migrant fleet  their distrust of outsiders and  inability to house members of other  species prevent cerberus operatives from  easily living  among them plus the quarian's  community-driven culture and loyalty to  one another prevent cerberus from paying  one of them off to be a spy  be sure to check out our lore video on  the quarians and the geth for more  information on their backstory  though cerberus works in the shadows  their name is well known by the events  of mass effect 1.  in 2165 so eight years after the first  contact war and  18 years prior to the start of mass  effect 1  cerberus became a public name when the  organization tried to steal antimatter  from the ssb geneva  an alliance cruiser five years later in  2170 in hopes of creating more human  biotics the elusive man  ordered cerberus operative paul grayson  to bomb an eldfield ashland energy  cruiser  in hopes its cargo of element zero would  blanket the colony of yandoa  and create more human biotics though the  incident caused a huge number of mental  and physical disabilities it did result  in 37 children developing biotic  abilities  deeming in an acceptable trade off  similar bombings incurred that same year  resulting in a large uptick of birth  defects as well as an increase in human  biotic births  over the next 12 years cerberus would  play a hand in several public  assassinations as well  including pope clement xvi in order to  ensure more human  leaders who approved of the cerberus  manifesto would reach political  and religious positions of power which  is why when shepard first hears the name  cerberus in 2183 the organization is  regarded by human and alien alike as a  terrorist group with racist pro-human  ideology  the elusive man and his dozen or so of  hand-picked project leads would disagree  arguing that they don't hate aliens they  largely preach that cerberus solely  exists to ensure humanity isn't stomped  out of existence  whether shepard trusts them on that is  up to you and that's the backstory into  cerberus creation  as well as the organization's brief  history between their foundation  and the events of mass effect 1. now  that mass effect legendary edition is  out and folks are playing the trilogy  again what cerberus project  most stands out in your mind when you  think of the organization for me  it's project eva responsible for the  creation of the infiltration combat mech  dr eva corey  we never learn why the elusive man named  one of his projects after one of his  dead mercenary companions  and i've always wondered let us know  what projects most stick out to you in  the comments and for more mass effect be  sure to subscribe  [Music]  you
 

